{:id "0014-shell-timestamps"
 :title "Shell: convert Firestore Timestamps before decoding (the app cannot read its conversation)"
 :lupa/deps #{"0011-app-shell"}
 :lupa/area :ui
 :lupa/risk :high
 :goal "The browser reads the seeded conversation, its members and messages.
        Today halfahead.fx.firebase/->wire converts a value with .toDate only
        when (object? v), and cljs.core/object? is true only for plain JS
        objects, never for a class instance like Firestore's Timestamp. So
        every timestamp reaches the codec unconverted, decode throws
        :ha/invalid-data for the conversation, and the page stays empty.
        Found by order 0013's reviewer running `bb e2e`."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/fx/firebase.cljs" "test/halfahead/fx/firebase_test.cljs"]
 :design "Split the conversion out of the snapshot handling:
            (data->wire data) — public; data is the JS object a snapshot's
            .data returns. Returns a string-keyed Clojure map in which every
            Firestore Timestamp (instance? of the Timestamp class imported
            from \"firebase/firestore\"), at any depth, inside maps or
            vectors, is a js/Date. Everything else as js->clj leaves it.
          ->wire calls (data->wire (.data snapshot #js {:serverTimestamps
          \"estimate\"})). Also log the codec's :errors with JSON.stringify so
          a decode failure names its fields in the console (the reviewer
          saw only `errors: Object`)."
 :acceptance
 ["A node test (test/halfahead/fx/firebase_test.cljs, picked up by the
   :test build) passes a plain JS object holding Timestamp.fromDate(d) at
   the top level, inside a nested map, and inside an array, and gets
   js/Dates equal to d at all three places"
  "Feeding data->wire's result for a conversation-shaped object (createdAt
   a Timestamp) to halfahead.codec/decode :ha/conversation succeeds"
  "Strings, numbers, booleans, nil, nested plain maps and arrays come
   through unchanged"
  "`bb test` stays green on all suites"]
 :non-goals
 ["Do not edit the codec, schema, core, views, or the app namespace"
  "No end-to-end test here (order 0013 re-runs after this)"]
 :context ["src/halfahead/fx/firebase.cljs" "src/halfahead/codec.cljc"
           "shadow-cljs.edn" "DESIGN.md"]
 :budget-usd 6.0}
